cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both this software and the associated article."
type: software
title: "Code for 'Hydrologic History Drives Divergent Soil Organic Matter Trajectories Across Hillslopes': R analysis pipeline for H.J. Andrews WS10 soil data"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/XTakver/HJA-WS10-Hydrologic-History"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R analysis code for the article "Hydrologic History Drives
  Divergent Soil Organic Matter Trajectories Across Hillslopes" (Journal of
  Geophysical Research: Biogeosciences). Processes, analyzes, and plots
  soil-moisture time series, FTICR-MS organic matter chemistry, soil
  biogeochemistry, vegetation, and soil physical properties from Watershed 10,
  H.J. Andrews Experimental Forest, Oregon, USA.
authors:
